# `git format-patch` output is byte-significant. Its context lines begin with a
# space — so a blank context line *is* trailing whitespace — and the `-- `
# signature separator and final newline are part of the format. Stripping any of
# it makes `git am` reject the patch, so whitespace checking and any end-of-line
# conversion are turned off here. Regenerate these files with format-patch; never
# hand-edit them.
patches/** -whitespace -text
